/* IT CHICK Academy · Arcade Japanese drills (Pass 26): Particle Pop and Sentence Builder, JLPT N5–N3.
   particles: ja has one （　） blank; ok is the one particle that fits; opts are 4 real particles.
   builder: tiles (particles attached), orders = every natural order (first = most natural).
   Furigana [漢字]{かな}: N5 items on every kanji; N4 on N4+ kanji; N3 on N3+ kanji and irregular readings. */
window.JPD = {
particles: [
  {id:"p5-001", lv:"N5", ja:"[毎日]{まいにち}、[日本語]{にほんご}の[本]{ほん}（　）[読]{よ}みます。", ok:"を", opts:["を","が","に","へ"], en:"I read a Japanese book every day.", why:"を marks the thing you read. が would make the book the one doing the reading; に and へ point to a place or goal, not the thing read."},
  {id:"p5-002", lv:"N5", ja:"トビーさんは[毎日]{まいにち}コーヒー（　）のみます。", ok:"を", opts:["を","が","に","へ"], en:"Toby drinks coffee every day.", why:"コーヒー is what Toby drinks, so it takes を. が is tempting because of コーヒーがすきです, but のみます is an action verb and its object takes を."},
  {id:"p5-003", lv:"N5", ja:"かいとさんは[山]{やま}のしゃしん（　）とりました。", ok:"を", opts:["を","が","で","に"], en:"Kaito took a photo of the mountain.", why:"しゃしんをとります: the photo is the object. で would say what you took it *with*, and there is no other object here."},
  {id:"p5-004", lv:"N5", ja:"イエンさんは[八時]{はちじ}にうち（　）[出]{で}ます。", ok:"を", opts:["を","に","で","が"], en:"Yến leaves home at eight.", why:"With [出]{で}ます, を marks the place you leave. に would mean going out *into* a place (そとに[出]{で}ます), the opposite direction."},
  {id:"p5-005", lv:"N5", ja:"あの[白]{しろ}いはし（　）わたって、[左]{ひだり}へ[行]{い}ってください。", ok:"を", opts:["を","に","で","が"], en:"Cross that white bridge and go left.", why:"わたります (cross) takes を for the thing you go across. で would mark where some other action happens; に is a goal, and you don't arrive *at* a bridge here."},
  {id:"p5-006", lv:"N5", ja:"[毎月]{まいつき}、[母]{はは}にてがみ（　）[書]{か}きます。", ok:"を", opts:["を","が","と","や"], en:"I write a letter to my mother every month.", why:"The letter is what you write: を. が would make the letter the writer; と and や join nouns into a list, and there is nothing to list."},
  {id:"p5-007", lv:"N5", ja:"トビーさんは[毎日]{まいにち}、[日本]{にほん}のニュース（　）[聞]{き}きます。", ok:"を", opts:["を","が","に","と"], en:"Toby listens to the Japanese news every day.", why:"[聞]{き}きます takes を for what you listen to. に with [聞]{き}きます means asking a person (せんせいに[聞]{き}きます), not listening to something."},
  {id:"p5-008", lv:"N5", ja:"すみません、そのあかいかさ（　）ください。", ok:"を", opts:["を","が","に","で"], en:"Excuse me, I'll take that red umbrella, please.", why:"〜をください: the thing you ask for takes を. Learners sometimes say がください by analogy with がほしいです, but ください needs を."},
  {id:"p5-009", lv:"N5", ja:"きのう、[友]{とも}だちと[日本]{にほん}のえいが（　）[見]{み}ました。", ok:"を", opts:["を","が","に","へ"], en:"Yesterday I watched a Japanese movie with a friend.", why:"The movie is what you watched, so を. [友]{とも}だちと already says who you were with; に or へ would turn the movie into a destination."},
  {id:"p5-010", lv:"N5", ja:"まりやさんは[毎日]{まいにち}、[日本語]{にほんご}でにっき（　）[書]{か}いています。", ok:"を", opts:["を","が","で","に"], en:"Mariya writes a diary in Japanese every day.", why:"にっき (diary) is what she writes: を. で is already used for the language ([日本語]{にほんご}で); a second で would make no sense."},
  {id:"p5-011", lv:"N5", ja:"あそこにねこ（　）います。", ok:"が", opts:["が","を","で","へ"], en:"There's a cat over there.", why:"With います/あります, the thing that exists takes が. を is for objects of action verbs, and いる has no object."},
  {id:"p5-012", lv:"N5", ja:"まりやさんはテニス（　）じょうずです。", ok:"が", opts:["が","を","に","で"], en:"Mariya is good at tennis.", why:"じょうず is an adjective, not an action, so the skill takes が: テニスがじょうずです. を is the usual mistake."},
  {id:"p5-013", lv:"N5", ja:"わたしはねこ（　）すきです。", ok:"が", opts:["が","を","に","で"], en:"I like cats.", why:"すき is a な-adjective; the thing you like takes が. ねこをすき is heard in casual speech but isn't standard; learn ねこがすきです."},
  {id:"p5-014", lv:"N5", ja:"[日本語]{にほんご}（　）すこしわかります。", ok:"が", opts:["が","を","で","に"], en:"I understand a little Japanese.", why:"わかります takes が for what is understood. [日本語]{にほんご}をわかります is a common mistake; [日本語]{にほんご}で would mean 'in Japanese'."},
  {id:"p5-015", lv:"N5", ja:"だれ（　）[来]{き}ましたか。", ok:"が", opts:["が","は","を","で"], en:"Who came?", why:"A question word as the subject always takes が. だれは is impossible: は marks something already known, and 'who' is exactly what you don't know."},
  {id:"p5-016", lv:"N5", ja:"どれ（　）イエンさんのかさですか。", ok:"が", opts:["が","は","を","に"], en:"Which one is Yến's umbrella?", why:"どれ is a question word, so it takes が, never は. The answer keeps が too: これがイエンさんのかさです."},
  {id:"p5-017", lv:"N5", ja:"[外]{そと}は[雨]{あめ}（　）ふっています。", ok:"が", opts:["が","を","で","に"], en:"It's raining outside.", why:"The rain is what falls, so it is the subject: [雨]{あめ}がふっています. を would make rain the object; で would make it the means."},
  {id:"p5-018", lv:"N5", ja:"[今日]{きょう}はあたま（　）いたいです。", ok:"が", opts:["が","を","に","で"], en:"I have a headache today.", why:"いたい is an adjective; the part that hurts takes が: あたまがいたいです. を is a common slip from English 'I hurt my head'."},
  {id:"p5-019", lv:"N5", ja:"わたしはあたらしいくるま（　）ほしいです。", ok:"が", opts:["が","を","に","で"], en:"I want a new car.", why:"ほしい is an adjective, so the thing you want takes が. Compare 〜たい with verbs, which allows を; ほしい does not in standard Japanese."},
  {id:"p5-020", lv:"N5", ja:"[学校]{がっこう}のとなりにこうえん（　）あります。", ok:"が", opts:["が","を","で","へ"], en:"There's a park next to the school.", why:"Place に + thing が + あります. で would mark where an action happens, and あります is not an action."},
  {id:"p5-021", lv:"N5", ja:"[日本]{にほん}とベトナムと、どちら（　）あついですか。", ok:"が", opts:["が","は","を","で"], en:"Which is hotter, Japan or Vietnam?", why:"どちら is a question word, so it takes が. どちらは is never possible."},
  {id:"p5-022", lv:"N5", ja:"どこ（　）いたいですか。", ok:"が", opts:["が","は","を","で"], en:"Where does it hurt?", why:"どこ is the subject of いたい, and question words take が. は can't follow a question word; を would make the place an object."},
  {id:"p5-023", lv:"N5", ja:"にくは[食]{た}べますが、さかな（　）[食]{た}べません。", ok:"は", opts:["は","が","も","に"], en:"I eat meat, but I don't eat fish.", why:"は sets fish against meat (contrast), which is exactly what 〜が (but) needs. も would mean 'fish too', which clashes with 'but'."},
  {id:"p5-024", lv:"N5", ja:"はじめまして。お[名前]{なまえ}（　）？", ok:"は", opts:["は","が","に","で"], en:"Nice to meet you. What's your name?", why:"お[名前]{なまえ}は？ means 'and your name?': は sets the topic, and the rest (なんですか) is left out. が can't hang at the end like this."},
  {id:"p5-025", lv:"N5", ja:"[今日]{きょう}（　）いいてんきですね。", ok:"は", opts:["は","が","を","に"], en:"It's nice weather today, isn't it?", why:"[今日]{きょう} is the topic: 'as for today, it's nice weather'. Time words like [今日]{きょう} take no に, and が would sound like 'it's TODAY that…'."},
  {id:"p5-026", lv:"N5", ja:"わたしは[毎日]{まいにち}[七時]{しちじ}（　）おきます。", ok:"に", opts:["に","で","を","が"], en:"I get up at seven every day.", why:"Clock times take に: [七時]{しちじ}におきます. で is a common mistake from English 'at'."},
  {id:"p5-027", lv:"N5", ja:"[友]{とも}だち（　）[電話]{でんわ}をかけます。", ok:"に", opts:["に","を","で","が"], en:"I'll call my friend.", why:"The person you phone takes に (the call goes *to* them). を is already on [電話]{でんわ}; a second を is not possible."},
  {id:"p5-028", lv:"N5", ja:"ねこはつくえの[下]{した}（　）います。", ok:"に", opts:["に","で","を","が"], en:"The cat is under the desk.", why:"Where something *is* takes に with います/あります. で is for where an action happens (つくえの[下]{した}でねます)."},
  {id:"p5-029", lv:"N5", ja:"わたしは[母]{はは}（　）はなをあげました。", ok:"に", opts:["に","が","を","で"], en:"I gave my mother flowers.", why:"The person who receives takes に with あげます. を is already on はな, and が would clash with わたしは as the giver."},
  {id:"p5-030", lv:"N5", ja:"としょかんへ[本]{ほん}をかえし（　）[行]{い}きます。", ok:"に", opts:["に","を","で","が"], en:"I'm going to the library to return a book.", why:"Verb stem + に + [行]{い}きます means 'go to do'. No other particle can follow a ます-stem like かえし."},
  {id:"p5-031", lv:"N5", ja:"へや（　）[入]{はい}るときは、くつをぬいでください。", ok:"に", opts:["に","を","で","が"], en:"Please take off your shoes when you go into the room.", why:"[入]{はい}ります takes に for the place you enter. へやを[入]{はい}る is a common mistake (を goes with [出]{で}ます, leaving)."},
  {id:"p5-032", lv:"N5", ja:"[毎日]{まいにち}、バス（　）のります。", ok:"に", opts:["に","を","で","が"], en:"I get on the bus every day.", why:"のります takes に: you get *onto* the bus. バスをのります is a very common learner error; バスで is for travelling by bus (バスで[行]{い}きます)."},
  {id:"p5-033", lv:"N5", ja:"あした、えきで[友]{とも}だち（　）あいます。", ok:"に", opts:["に","を","で","が"], en:"Tomorrow I'm meeting a friend at the station.", why:"あいます takes に for the person you meet (と works too, so it isn't offered). を is the classic mistake from English 'meet someone'."},
  {id:"p5-034", lv:"N5", ja:"わたしはしおうら（　）すんでいます。", ok:"に", opts:["に","で","を","へ"], en:"I live in Shioura.", why:"すんでいます takes に for where you live. で is tempting ('in'), but すむ is about being somewhere, like います, so it takes に."},
  {id:"p5-035", lv:"N5", ja:"どようび（　）[友]{とも}だちと[山]{やま}へ[行]{い}きます。", ok:"に", opts:["に","で","を","が"], en:"On Saturday I'm going to the mountains with friends.", why:"Days of the week take に: どようびに. で is wrong for points in time. (Words like きのう, [今日]{きょう}, あした take no particle at all.)"},
  {id:"p5-036", lv:"N5", ja:"ここ（　）[名前]{なまえ}を[書]{か}いてください。", ok:"に", opts:["に","を","が","と"], en:"Please write your name here.", why:"に marks where the writing ends up (on this spot). を is already on [名前]{なまえ}; が and と can't mark a place."},
  {id:"p5-037", lv:"N5", ja:"トビーさんはあおいさん（　）えいごをおしえます。", ok:"に", opts:["に","を","で","が"], en:"Toby teaches Aoi English.", why:"The person you teach takes に; the subject taught takes を. あおいさんを would leave two を in one sentence."},
  {id:"p5-038", lv:"N5", ja:"[毎日]{まいにち}、としょかん（　）べんきょうします。", ok:"で", opts:["で","に","を","へ"], en:"I study at the library every day.", why:"Studying is an action, so its place takes で. に is for where something *is* (としょかんにいます)."},
  {id:"p5-039", lv:"N5", ja:"ロドリゴさんはバス（　）[学校]{がっこう}へ[行]{い}きます。", ok:"で", opts:["で","に","を","と"], en:"Rodrigo goes to school by bus.", why:"で marks the means: バスで. バスに would mean getting *on* the bus, which needs のります."},
  {id:"p5-040", lv:"N5", ja:"はし（　）ごはんを[食]{た}べます。", ok:"で", opts:["で","を","に","と"], en:"I eat rice with chopsticks.", why:"The tool you use takes で. を is already on ごはん; と would mean 'together with chopsticks', as if they were a person."},
  {id:"p5-041", lv:"N5", ja:"[日本語]{にほんご}（　）[名前]{なまえ}を[書]{か}いてください。", ok:"で", opts:["で","を","に","が"], en:"Please write your name in Japanese.", why:"A language used as a means takes で. を is already on [名前]{なまえ}."},
  {id:"p5-042", lv:"N5", ja:"きのう、コンビニ（　）パンをかいました。", ok:"で", opts:["で","に","を","へ"], en:"Yesterday I bought bread at the convenience store.", why:"Buying is an action, so the place takes で. コンビニにパンをかいました is a very common mistake."},
  {id:"p5-043", lv:"N5", ja:"このりんごは[三]{みっ}つ（　）[五百円]{ごひゃくえん}です。", ok:"で", opts:["で","に","を","と"], en:"These apples are three for 500 yen.", why:"で after a quantity gives the total: [三]{みっ}つで = 'three together'. に and を can't do this."},
  {id:"p5-044", lv:"N5", ja:"[日本]{にほん}の[食]{た}べもの（　）[何]{なに}がいちばんすきですか。", ok:"で", opts:["で","に","を","が"], en:"What's your favourite Japanese food?", why:"で sets the group you choose from: '(among) Japanese foods, what do you like most?' が is already on [何]{なに}."},
  {id:"p5-045", lv:"N5", ja:"なつやすみに、うみ（　）およぎました。", ok:"で", opts:["で","に","が","と"], en:"I swam in the sea during the summer holidays.", why:"Swimming is an action, so where it happens takes で. に would mean going *into* the sea as a destination."},
  {id:"p5-046", lv:"N5", ja:"[日本]{にほん}（　）いちばん[高]{たか}い[山]{やま}はふじさんです。", ok:"で", opts:["で","に","を","が"], en:"The highest mountain in Japan is Mt Fuji.", why:"で sets the range for 'the most': [日本]{にほん}でいちばん. に would say where the mountain *is*, which doesn't fit with いちばん."},
  {id:"p5-047", lv:"N5", ja:"このへや（　）たばこをすわないでください。", ok:"で", opts:["で","に","を","が"], en:"Please don't smoke in this room.", why:"Smoking is an action, so the place takes で. を is already on たばこ."},
  {id:"p5-048", lv:"N5", ja:"いいてんきですから、[外]{そと}（　）あそびましょう。", ok:"で", opts:["で","に","を","へ"], en:"It's nice weather, so let's play outside.", why:"あそびます is an action: [外]{そと}で. [外]{そと}に or [外]{そと}へ would need a movement verb ([外]{そと}に[出]{で}ます)."},
  {id:"p5-049", lv:"N5", ja:"わたしは[来年]{らいねん}、[国]{くに}（　）かえります。", ok:"へ", opts:["へ","で","が","と"], en:"I'm going back to my country next year.", why:"へ marks the direction you go in. (に also works with かえります, so it isn't offered.) で would mark a place of action, and と would mean 'with my country'."},
  {id:"p5-050", lv:"N5", ja:"あおいさんは[電車]{でんしゃ}でとうきょう（　）[行]{い}きました。", ok:"へ", opts:["へ","を","で","と"], en:"Aoi went to Tokyo by train.", why:"へ marks where you are heading. で is already used for the means ([電車]{でんしゃ}で); を with [行]{い}きます would mean going *along* a route."},
  {id:"p5-051", lv:"N5", ja:"きのう、[友]{とも}だち（　）えいがを[見]{み}ました。", ok:"と", opts:["と","に","を","で"], en:"Yesterday I watched a movie with a friend.", why:"と marks the person you do something with. を is already on えいが; に would make your friend a target."},
  {id:"p5-052", lv:"N5", ja:"スーパーでパン（　）たまごをかいました。", ok:"と", opts:["と","を","で","に"], en:"I bought bread and eggs at the supermarket.", why:"と joins nouns: パンとたまご (that's all you bought). を comes only once, after the last item."},
  {id:"p5-053", lv:"N5", ja:"トビーさんはロドリゴさん（　）テニスをします。", ok:"と", opts:["と","に","を","が"], en:"Toby plays tennis with Rodrigo.", why:"と = 'with (a partner)'. に would make Rodrigo the target, as if Toby did tennis *to* him."},
  {id:"p5-054", lv:"N5", ja:"まりやさんのお[父]{とう}さん（　）お[母]{かあ}さんはしおじまにいます。", ok:"と", opts:["と","が","を","に"], en:"Mariya's father and mother live on Shiojima.", why:"と joins the two nouns into one subject. が here would leave お[母]{かあ}さんは with no place in the sentence."},
  {id:"p5-055", lv:"N5", ja:"このかばんは、わたしのかばん（　）おなじです。", ok:"と", opts:["と","に","を","で"], en:"This bag is the same as my bag.", why:"おなじ takes と for the thing compared: 〜とおなじ. に is a common slip; を and で don't fit."},
  {id:"p5-056", lv:"N5", ja:"わたしは[学生]{がくせい}です。まりやさん（　）[学生]{がくせい}です。", ok:"も", opts:["も","を","に","で"], en:"I'm a student. Mariya is a student too.", why:"も = 'too': it replaces は when the same thing is true again. を, に and で can't mark who something is."},
  {id:"p5-057", lv:"N5", ja:"[今日]{きょう}は[何]{なに}（　）[食]{た}べませんでした。", ok:"も", opts:["も","が","を","に"], en:"I didn't eat anything today.", why:"Question word + も + negative = 'nothing at all'. [何]{なに}を is only for asking 'what?'."},
  {id:"p5-058", lv:"N5", ja:"きのうのパーティーには、だれ（　）[来]{き}ませんでした。", ok:"も", opts:["も","が","に","を"], en:"Nobody came to the party yesterday.", why:"だれも + negative = 'nobody'. だれが is for questions (だれが[来]{き}ましたか), so it can't end a statement like this."},
  {id:"p5-059", lv:"N5", ja:"この[本]{ほん}（　）あの[本]{ほん}もおもしろいです。", ok:"も", opts:["も","が","を","に"], en:"Both this book and that book are interesting.", why:"AもBも = 'both A and B'. The second も is already there, so the first one must be も too."},
  {id:"p5-060", lv:"N5", ja:"これはイエンさん（　）かさです。", ok:"の", opts:["の","が","は","を"], en:"This is Yến's umbrella.", why:"の joins two nouns: イエンさんのかさ = 'Yến's umbrella'. が and は can't link a noun to the next noun."},
  {id:"p5-061", lv:"N5", ja:"[日本語]{にほんご}（　）[先生]{せんせい}はどのかたですか。", ok:"の", opts:["の","を","が","で"], en:"Which person is the Japanese teacher?", why:"[日本語]{にほんご}の[先生]{せんせい} = 'a teacher of Japanese'. を is tempting because the teacher teaches Japanese, but a noun before a noun needs の."},
  {id:"p5-062", lv:"N5", ja:"あの[白]{しろ}いかばんはだれ（　）ですか。", ok:"の", opts:["の","が","を","に"], en:"Whose is that white bag?", why:"だれの = 'whose' (the noun かばん is understood). だれが would ask who *does* something."},
  {id:"p5-063", lv:"N5", ja:"[大学]{だいがく}（　）[前]{まえ}にカフェがあります。", ok:"の", opts:["の","が","を","で"], en:"There's a café in front of the university.", why:"Place words like [前]{まえ}, [上]{うえ} and [中]{なか} join the noun with の: [大学]{だいがく}の[前]{まえ}."},
  {id:"p5-064", lv:"N5", ja:"[学校]{がっこう}は[九時]{くじ}（　）です。", ok:"から", opts:["から","に","で","を"], en:"School starts at nine.", why:"〜からです = 'it's from…' (when something starts). に would need a verb after it (はじまります). (まで also fits here, so it isn't offered.)"},
  {id:"p5-065", lv:"N5", ja:"トビーさんはオーストラリア（　）[来]{き}ました。", ok:"から", opts:["から","を","で","が"], en:"Toby came from Australia.", why:"から marks where you start from. を with [来]{き}ます would mean coming *along* a route, and で marks a place of action."},
  {id:"p5-066", lv:"N5", ja:"[雨]{あめ}です（　）、タクシーで[行]{い}きましょう。", ok:"から", opts:["から","まで","と","を"], en:"It's raining, so let's go by taxi.", why:"Sentence + から gives a reason: 'because it's raining'. まで is for limits in time or space, not reasons."},
  {id:"p5-067", lv:"N5", ja:"うち（　）[学校]{がっこう}まで[十分]{じゅっぷん}です。", ok:"から", opts:["から","に","で","を"], en:"It's ten minutes from my home to school.", why:"AからBまで = 'from A to B'. まで is already there, so the start needs から."},
  {id:"p5-068", lv:"N5", ja:"[九時]{くじ}から[五時]{ごじ}（　）はたらきます。", ok:"まで", opts:["まで","に","で","へ"], en:"I work from nine to five.", why:"から…まで = 'from… until…'. に would give a single point in time, not the end of a stretch."},
  {id:"p5-069", lv:"N5", ja:"えき（　）あるいて[十分]{じゅっぷん}ぐらいです。", ok:"まで", opts:["まで","で","を","が"], en:"It's about ten minutes' walk to the station.", why:"まで = 'as far as': the distance to the station. で would mark a place where something happens, and を would make the station an object."},
  {id:"p5-070", lv:"N5", ja:"[一]{いち}から[十]{じゅう}（　）かぞえてください。", ok:"まで", opts:["まで","に","へ","で"], en:"Please count from one to ten.", why:"から…まで again: the count stops at ten. へ is a direction of movement, not the end of a series."},
  {id:"p5-071", lv:"N5", ja:"バスは[電車]{でんしゃ}（　）やすいです。", ok:"より", opts:["より","から","と","に"], en:"The bus is cheaper than the train.", why:"より = 'than'. から is 'from', a common confusion because both can follow the second item."},
  {id:"p5-072", lv:"N5", ja:"[日本]{にほん}のなつは、わたしの[国]{くに}のなつ（　）あついです。", ok:"より", opts:["より","から","まで","と"], en:"Summer in Japan is hotter than summer back home.", why:"Xより = 'than X'. まで and から give limits, not comparisons."},
  {id:"p5-073", lv:"N5", ja:"かばんの[中]{なか}に[本]{ほん}（　）ノートなどがあります。", ok:"や", opts:["や","の","を","で"], en:"In the bag there are books, notebooks and so on.", why:"や gives examples from a longer list, and goes with など. の would make 'the book's notebook'."},
  {id:"p5-074", lv:"N5", ja:"やすみの[日]{ひ}は、そうじ（　）せんたくをします。", ok:"や", opts:["や","を","が","で"], en:"On my days off I do cleaning, laundry and things like that.", why:"や lists examples (there may be more). を comes only once, after the last item."},
  {id:"p5-075", lv:"N5", ja:"これは[何]{なん}です（　）。", ok:"か", opts:["か","ね","よ","と"], en:"What is this?", why:"か makes a question. ね asks for agreement and よ tells news; neither fits a 'what?' question."},
  {id:"p5-076", lv:"N5", ja:"あした（　）あさって、いっしょに[山]{やま}へ[行]{い}きませんか。", ok:"か", opts:["か","も","の","を"], en:"Would you like to go to the mountains together tomorrow or the day after?", why:"AかB = 'A or B'. も would need a second も (あしたもあさっても), and の would make 'tomorrow's day after'."},
  {id:"p5-077", lv:"N5", ja:"あ、だれ（　）[来]{き}ましたよ。", ok:"か", opts:["か","が","も","を"], en:"Oh, someone's here.", why:"だれか = 'someone'. だれが asks 'who?', which can't end in よ; だれも needs a negative verb."},
  {id:"p5-078", lv:"N5", ja:"おはようございます。[今日]{きょう}はさむいです（　）。", ok:"ね", opts:["ね","よ","か","を"], en:"Good morning. It's cold today, isn't it?", why:"ね invites agreement about something you both feel. よ would tell the other person news they already know; か would ask whether it's cold."},
  {id:"p5-079", lv:"N5", ja:"A：このケーキ、[食]{た}べてもいいですか。B：ええ、いいです（　）。どうぞ。", ok:"よ", opts:["よ","か","を","に"], en:"A: May I eat this cake? B: Yes, sure. Go ahead.", why:"よ gives the other person information they don't have: 'Yes, you may'. か would turn B's answer back into a question, and を and に can't end a sentence."},
  {id:"p5-080", lv:"N5", ja:"A：えきはどこですか。B：あそこです（　）。", ok:"よ", opts:["よ","か","と","を"], en:"A: Where is the station? B: It's over there.", why:"B tells A something new, so よ. か would turn the answer into a question, and と and を can't end a sentence."},
  {id:"p4-001", lv:"N4", ja:"さいふに百円（　）ありません。", ok:"しか", opts:["しか","だけ","ばかり","ほど"], en:"I only have 100 yen in my wallet.", why:"しか + negative = 'only'. だけ also means 'only', but it goes with a positive verb (百円だけあります); 百円だけありません would mean 'only 100 yen is missing'."},
  {id:"p4-002", lv:"N4", ja:"日本語は[少]{すこ}し（　）話せません。", ok:"しか", opts:["しか","だけ","ばかり","ほど"], en:"I can only speak a little Japanese.", why:"The verb is negative, so 'only' must be しか. With だけ you'd say [少]{すこ}しだけ[話]{はな}せます."},
  {id:"p4-003", lv:"N4", ja:"きのうは三時間（　）ねられませんでした。", ok:"しか", opts:["しか","だけ","より","まで"], en:"Last night I could only sleep for three hours.", why:"しか…ない: only three hours. だけ needs a positive verb (三時間だけねました); まで would say until when, and より is for comparing."},
  {id:"p4-004", lv:"N4", ja:"パーティーには一人（　）[来]{こ}なかった。", ok:"しか", opts:["しか","だけ","ばかり","ほど"], en:"Only one person came to the party.", why:"一人しか[来]{こ}なかった = only one came. Watch out: 一人だけ[来]{こ}なかった means the opposite, 'only one person *didn't* come'."},
  {id:"p4-005", lv:"N4", ja:"この[店]{みせ}はげんきん（　）[使]{つか}えません。カードはだめです。", ok:"しか", opts:["しか","だけ","ほど","ばかり"], en:"This shop only takes cash. Cards are no good.", why:"しか + negative: cash is the only thing you can use. げんきんだけ[使]{つか}えません would mean cash is the one thing you *can't* use, which the next sentence contradicts."},
  {id:"p4-006", lv:"N4", ja:"今日は一時間（　）[勉強]{べんきょう}しました。", ok:"だけ", opts:["だけ","しか","まで","を"], en:"Today I studied for just one hour.", why:"だけ = 'just, only' with a positive verb. しか would need a negative ([勉強]{べんきょう}しませんでした)."},
  {id:"p4-007", lv:"N4", ja:"ここには名前（　）書けばいいです。ほかは書かなくてもいいです。", ok:"だけ", opts:["だけ","しか","ばかり","ほど"], en:"You only need to write your name here. You don't have to fill in the rest.", why:"だけ marks the one thing needed, with a positive verb. しか can't go with 書けばいい (no negative)."},
  {id:"p4-008", lv:"N4", ja:"みんな[知]{し}っていたのに、[私]{わたし}（　）[知]{し}らなかったんですか。", ok:"だけ", opts:["だけ","ばかり","ほど","って"], en:"Everyone knew, and I was the only one who didn't?", why:"[私]{わたし}だけ = 'only me'. だけ works with a negative verb when *that person* is the exception. ばかり means 'nothing but', which doesn't fit one person."},
  {id:"p4-009", lv:"N4", ja:"すみません、ちょっと見る（　）です。", ok:"だけ", opts:["だけ","しか","ばかり","ほど"], en:"Sorry, I'm just looking.", why:"Verb + だけです = 'I'm just doing…'. しか needs a negative verb, and [見]{み}るばかりです would mean you do nothing *but* look, all the time."},
  {id:"p4-010", lv:"N4", ja:"トビーさんはこのごろ、ラーメン（　）食べています。", ok:"ばかり", opts:["ばかり","しか","ほど","より"], en:"Toby has been eating nothing but ramen lately.", why:"ばかり = 'nothing but, all the time' (often a complaint). しか needs a negative verb; より is for comparing."},
  {id:"p4-011", lv:"N4", ja:"[弟]{おとうと}はゲーム（　）していて、ぜんぜん[勉強]{べんきょう}しない。", ok:"ばかり", opts:["ばかり","しか","ほど","より"], en:"My little brother does nothing but play games and never studies.", why:"ばかり: games and only games, again and again. しか would need していない, and より compares two things."},
  {id:"p4-012", lv:"N4", ja:"[今週]{こんしゅう}は雨（　）で、せんたくものがかわかない。", ok:"ばかり", opts:["ばかり","しか","ほど","だけ"], en:"It's been nothing but rain this week, so the laundry won't dry.", why:"Noun + ばかりで = 'it's all…'. しか needs a negative; [雨]{あめ}だけで would mean 'with rain alone', which doesn't explain the laundry."},
  {id:"p4-013", lv:"N4", ja:"かいとさんは食べて（　）いないで、[少]{すこ}しは[運動]{うんどう}したほうがいい。", ok:"ばかり", opts:["ばかり","しか","だけ","ほど"], en:"Kaito shouldn't just eat all the time; he should get a bit of exercise.", why:"〜てばかりいる = 'do nothing but…'. てしかいない and てだけいない are not patterns."},
  {id:"p4-014", lv:"N4", ja:"[今年]{ことし}の[夏]{なつ}は[去年]{きょねん}（　）あつくない。", ok:"ほど", opts:["ほど","しか","だけ","ばかり"], en:"This summer isn't as hot as last year.", why:"Xほど〜ない = 'not as… as X'. しか…ない would mean 'only', which makes no sense with a comparison."},
  {id:"p4-015", lv:"N4", ja:"N4の[試験]{しけん}は[思]{おも}った（　）むずかしくなかった。", ok:"ほど", opts:["ほど","だけ","しか","ばかり"], en:"The N4 test wasn't as hard as I thought.", why:"[思]{おも}ったほど〜ない = 'not as… as I thought'. だけ and ばかり mean 'only', not 'as… as'."},
  {id:"p4-016", lv:"N4", ja:"このへんには、あの[店]{みせ}（　）おいしいラーメン[屋]{や}はありません。", ok:"ほど", opts:["ほど","だけ","を","ばかり"], en:"Around here there's no ramen shop as good as that one.", why:"Xほど〜はない = 'nothing is as… as X' (praise for X). だけ and ばかり mean 'only', which doesn't compare anything; を can't mark the shop you compare with."},
  {id:"p4-017", lv:"N4", ja:"休みの日は[映画]{えいが}（　）[買]{か}い[物]{もの}とか、いろいろしています。", ok:"とか", opts:["とか","しか","ほど","ばかり"], en:"On my days off I do all sorts of things, like movies and shopping.", why:"AとかBとか gives examples, casually. The second とか is already there, so the first one must match. しか and ほど don't list things."},
  {id:"p4-018", lv:"N4", ja:"スポーツはサッカー（　）テニスとかがすきです。", ok:"とか", opts:["とか","しか","ばかり","ほど"], en:"For sports, I like things like football and tennis.", why:"とか…とか lists examples in casual speech. ばかり would mean 'nothing but football', which can't be followed by テニスとか."},
  {id:"p4-019", lv:"N4", ja:"日本の[料理]{りょうり}なら、すし（　）てんぷらとか、何でもすきです。", ok:"とか", opts:["とか","だけ","ほど","しか"], en:"When it comes to Japanese food, I like anything: sushi, tempura and so on.", why:"とか gives examples from a longer list (何でも = anything). だけ would mean 'only sushi', which clashes with 何でも."},
  {id:"p4-020", lv:"N4", ja:"「かもめ」（　）、どういう[意味]{いみ}ですか。", ok:"って", opts:["って","が","を","で"], en:"What does 'kamome' mean?", why:"って is the casual way to raise a word as the topic ('this word kamome…'). (は also works, so it isn't offered.) が and を don't fit before どういう[意味]{いみ}ですか."},
  {id:"p4-021", lv:"N4", ja:"あおいさんは今日[来]{こ}られない（　）[言]{い}っていました。", ok:"って", opts:["って","か","が","ほど"], en:"Aoi said she can't come today.", why:"って is spoken と for quoting: 〜って[言]{い}っていました. (と also works, so it isn't offered.) か would make it a question, and there's no question word."},
  {id:"p4-022", lv:"N4", ja:"ロドリゴさん（　）、ほんとうにえがうまいね。", ok:"って", opts:["って","を","と","に"], en:"Rodrigo is really good at drawing, isn't he?", why:"って marks the topic in casual speech, like は. を and に can't mark the person being described; と would mean 'with Rodrigo'."},
  {id:"p4-023", lv:"N4", ja:"電車でとなりの人（　）[足]{あし}をふまれました。", ok:"に", opts:["に","を","で","と"], en:"On the train, the person next to me stepped on my foot.", why:"In a passive sentence, the person who does the action takes に. を is already on [足]{あし}; で is already used for the place."},
  {id:"p4-024", lv:"N4", ja:"[私]{わたし}は先生（　）ほめられました。", ok:"に", opts:["に","が","を","で"], en:"I was praised by my teacher.", why:"Passive: the doer takes に. 先生が would make the teacher the subject, but the subject is already [私]{わたし}は."},
  {id:"p4-025", lv:"N4", ja:"かえり[道]{みち}で雨（　）ふられて、かぜをひきました。", ok:"に", opts:["に","が","を","で"], en:"I got caught in the rain on the way home and caught a cold.", why:"This is the 'suffering' passive: [雨]{あめ}にふられる = 'be rained on'. [雨]{あめ}が needs the active verb ふって."},
  {id:"p4-026", lv:"N4", ja:"母は[弟]{おとうと}（　）へやのそうじをさせました。", ok:"に", opts:["に","を","が","で"], en:"My mother made my little brother clean his room.", why:"In a causative with an object (そうじを), the person made to act takes に, because Japanese avoids two を in one clause."},
  {id:"p4-027", lv:"N4", ja:"かいとさんはおもしろい話をして、みんな（　）わらわせました。", ok:"を", opts:["を","に","が","と"], en:"Kaito told a funny story and made everyone laugh.", why:"With a verb like わらう that has no object, the person made to act usually takes を. に suggests 'let them laugh', which doesn't fit a joke."},
  {id:"p4-028", lv:"N4", ja:"かいとさんは来年、二十さい（　）なります。", ok:"に", opts:["に","を","が","で"], en:"Kaito will turn twenty next year.", why:"Noun + になる = 'become'. を and が can't mark what something becomes."},
  {id:"p4-029", lv:"N4", ja:"[図書館]{としょかん}の中では、しずか（　）してください。", ok:"に", opts:["に","で","を","が"], en:"Please be quiet in the library.", why:"な-adjective + にする = 'make it…, be…'. で is the て-form of です, which can't come before する."},
  {id:"p4-030", lv:"N4", ja:"[一週間]{いっしゅうかん}（　）さんかい、プールでおよぎます。", ok:"に", opts:["に","を","と","が"], en:"I swim at the pool three times a week.", why:"Period + に + number = 'X times per period'. を and と can't give 'per'."},
  {id:"p4-031", lv:"N4", ja:"[来週]{らいしゅう}、きょうとへ[旅行]{りょこう}（　）行きます。", ok:"に", opts:["に","を","が","と"], en:"I'm going on a trip to Kyoto next week.", why:"Noun of activity + に + 行く = 'go to do it'. [旅行]{りょこう}を行く is not Japanese (it would need する: [旅行]{りょこう}をする)."},
  {id:"p4-032", lv:"N4", ja:"[私]{わたし}はまりやさん（　）ケーキをもらいました。", ok:"に", opts:["に","が","を","と"], en:"I got a cake from Mariya.", why:"With もらう, the giver takes に (or から, so it isn't offered). が would clash with [私]{わたし}は as the receiver."},
  {id:"p4-033", lv:"N4", ja:"[私]{わたし}は友だち（　）[駅]{えき}まで[送]{おく}ってもらいました。", ok:"に", opts:["に","が","で","へ"], en:"I got my friend to take me to the station.", why:"〜てもらう: the person who does the favour takes に. が would clash with [私]{わたし}は, the person who receives it."},
  {id:"p4-034", lv:"N4", ja:"山が見えるへや（　）しました。", ok:"に", opts:["に","を","が","で"], en:"I decided on a room with a view of the mountains.", why:"〜にする = 'decide on, choose'. へやをしました is not a pattern; を is used with する only for actions ([勉強]{べんきょう}をする)."},
  {id:"p4-035", lv:"N4", ja:"この[道]{みち}（　）まっすぐ行くと、[駅]{えき}があります。", ok:"を", opts:["を","で","に","が"], en:"If you go straight along this road, you'll come to the station.", why:"With movement verbs, を marks the route you move along. で would mark a place where an action happens, not a route."},
  {id:"p4-036", lv:"N4", ja:"トビーさんは三月に[大学院]{だいがくいん}（　）そつぎょうします。", ok:"を", opts:["を","に","で","が"], en:"Toby graduates from his graduate school in March.", why:"そつぎょうする takes を for the school you leave (like [出]{で}る). で would mark a place of action; に a destination."},
  {id:"p4-037", lv:"N4", ja:"こうえんの前でバス（　）おりて、[少]{すこ}し[歩]{ある}きました。", ok:"を", opts:["を","に","で","へ"], en:"I got off the bus in front of the park and walked a little.", why:"おりる takes を (or から) for what you get off. バスに is for getting *on* (のる); で is already on the place."},
  {id:"p4-038", lv:"N4", ja:"[風]{かぜ}でドア（　）[開]{あ}きました。", ok:"が", opts:["が","を","に","で"], en:"The door opened in the wind.", why:"[開]{あ}く is intransitive (the door opens by itself), so the door is the subject: が. を goes with transitive [開]{あ}ける."},
  {id:"p4-039", lv:"N4", ja:"あ、まりやさんのへやの電気（　）ついていますね。", ok:"が", opts:["が","を","に","で"], en:"Oh, the light is on in Mariya's room.", why:"つく is intransitive, so the light is the subject: が. を needs transitive つける ([電気]{でんき}をつける)."},
  {id:"p4-040", lv:"N4", ja:"つくえの上に[花]{はな}（　）かざってあります。", ok:"が", opts:["が","で","と","へ"], en:"Flowers have been put on the desk (for display).", why:"〜てある describes a state someone left; the thing usually takes が. で would make the desk a place of action, which clashes with に."},
  {id:"p4-041", lv:"N4", ja:"ここから[海]{うみ}（　）見えます。", ok:"が", opts:["が","を","で","へ"], en:"You can see the sea from here.", why:"見える ('can be seen') takes が. を goes with 見る, not 見える."},
  {id:"p4-042", lv:"N4", ja:"となりのへやから[音楽]{おんがく}（　）聞こえます。", ok:"が", opts:["が","を","で","に"], en:"I can hear music from the next room.", why:"聞こえる ('can be heard') takes が, like 見える. を is for 聞く."},
  {id:"p4-043", lv:"N4", ja:"[私]{わたし}（　）[作]{つく}ったケーキを食べてください。", ok:"が", opts:["が","は","を","に"], en:"Please eat the cake I made.", why:"Inside a clause that describes a noun (〜[作]{つく}ったケーキ), the subject takes が (or の), never は."},
  {id:"p4-044", lv:"N4", ja:"まりやさん（　）[私]{わたし}にケーキをくれました。", ok:"が", opts:["が","を","に","で"], en:"Mariya gave me a cake.", why:"With くれる the giver is the subject: が (or は). に is already on [私]{わたし}, the receiver."},
  {id:"p4-045", lv:"N4", ja:"バスより電車の[方]{ほう}（　）[早]{はや}いです。", ok:"が", opts:["が","を","で","に"], en:"The train is faster than the bus.", why:"〜の[方]{ほう}が = 'the… one is more'. The pattern is fixed: XよりYの[方]{ほう}が."},
  {id:"p4-046", lv:"N4", ja:"母（　）[作]{つく}るカレーは[世界]{せかい}でいちばんおいしい。", ok:"の", opts:["の","は","を","で"], en:"The curry my mother makes is the best in the world.", why:"In a clause describing a noun, the subject can take の instead of が: [母]{はは}の[作]{つく}るカレー. は can't be used inside the clause."},
  {id:"p4-047", lv:"N4", ja:"[私]{わたし}は[料理]{りょうり}を[作]{つく}る（　）がすきです。", ok:"の", opts:["の","を","に","と"], en:"I like cooking.", why:"の turns a verb into a noun ('making food') so it can take が. を, に and と can't do this."},
  {id:"p4-048", lv:"N4", ja:"これは母へ（　）プレゼントです。", ok:"の", opts:["の","を","が","に"], en:"This is a present for my mother.", why:"へ + の joins a direction to a noun: [母]{はは}へのプレゼント. へを and へが don't exist."},
  {id:"p4-049", lv:"N4", ja:"かぜ（　）学校を休みました。", ok:"で", opts:["で","に","を","が"], en:"I missed school because of a cold.", why:"Noun + で can give a cause: かぜで = 'because of a cold'. を is already on 学校."},
  {id:"p4-050", lv:"N4", ja:"[台風]{たいふう}（　）電車が[止]{と}まりました。", ok:"で", opts:["で","に","を","と"], en:"The trains stopped because of the typhoon.", why:"で gives the cause. [台風]{たいふう}に would need a passive verb; を can't go with intransitive [止]{と}まる."},
  {id:"p4-051", lv:"N4", ja:"この[仕事]{しごと}は一時間（　）[終]{お}わります。", ok:"で", opts:["で","に","を","まで"], en:"This job will be finished in an hour.", why:"Time + で = 'within, taking': 一時間で. に would need a clock time (三時に), and まで would mean 'until'."},
  {id:"p4-052", lv:"N4", ja:"レポートは[金曜日]{きんようび}（　）出してください。", ok:"までに", opts:["までに","まで","から","で"], en:"Please hand in your report by Friday.", why:"までに = 'by' (a deadline for one action). まで = 'until' and needs an action that goes on (五時まで[待]{ま}つ)."},
  {id:"p4-053", lv:"N4", ja:"五時（　）ここで[待]{ま}っています。", ok:"まで", opts:["まで","までに","で","を"], en:"I'll wait here until five.", why:"Waiting goes on, so 'until' = まで. までに is for one action done before a deadline."},
  {id:"p4-054", lv:"N4", ja:"[夏休]{なつやす}み（　）この本を読んでおいてください。", ok:"までに", opts:["までに","まで","から","で"], en:"Please read this book before the summer holidays.", why:"〜までに = 'by' a deadline. まで with 読んでおく would mean reading nonstop until then."},
  {id:"p4-055", lv:"N4", ja:"このボタンをおす（　）、水が出ます。", ok:"と", opts:["と","が","を","に"], en:"When you press this button, water comes out.", why:"Plain verb + と = 'whenever / if (always)': a natural result. が would mean 'but', which doesn't fit."},
  {id:"p4-056", lv:"N4", ja:"[明日]{あした}は雨だ（　）[思]{おも}います。", ok:"と", opts:["と","を","が","に"], en:"I think it will rain tomorrow.", why:"と marks what you think or say: 〜と[思]{おも}います. を is a common mistake from English 'think something'."},
  {id:"p4-057", lv:"N4", ja:"コンサートは何時に[始]{はじ}まる（　）[知]{し}っていますか。", ok:"か", opts:["か","と","が","を"], en:"Do you know what time the concert starts?", why:"A question inside a sentence ends in か. と would need a fact, not a question word like 何時."},
  {id:"p4-058", lv:"N4", ja:"パーティーに行く（　）どうか、まだきめていません。", ok:"か", opts:["か","と","が","の"], en:"I haven't decided yet whether I'll go to the party.", why:"〜かどうか = 'whether or not'. It is a fixed pattern; nothing else can come before どうか."},
  {id:"p4-059", lv:"N4", ja:"[駅]{えき}で一時間（　）[待]{ま}ちました。", ok:"も", opts:["も","しか","を","に"], en:"I waited at the station for a whole hour.", why:"Number + も = 'as much as' (more than expected). しか needs a negative verb; に can't follow a length of time."},
  {id:"p4-060", lv:"N4", ja:"ケーキを五つ（　）食べたんですか！", ok:"も", opts:["も","しか","を","に"], en:"You ate five pieces of cake?!", why:"も after a number shows surprise at how many. を is already on ケーキ, and しか would need a negative verb."},
  {id:"p3-001", lv:"N3", ja:"[忙]{いそが}しくて、昼ご飯を食べる時間（　）なかった。", ok:"さえ", opts:["さえ","こそ","ばかり","として"], en:"I was so busy I didn't even have time to eat lunch.", why:"さえ = 'even' (the most basic thing was missing). こそ picks out one thing for praise or emphasis and doesn't go with this kind of negative."},
  {id:"p3-002", lv:"N3", ja:"この漢字は小学生（　）読めますよ。", ok:"さえ", opts:["さえ","など","ばかり","として"], en:"Even primary school kids can read this kanji.", why:"さえ = 'even': if children can, so can you. など would look down on the children, and ばかり means 'nothing but'."},
  {id:"p3-003", lv:"N3", ja:"時間（　）あれば、もっと旅行したいんですが。", ok:"さえ", opts:["さえ","こそ","しか","ばかり"], en:"If only I had the time, I'd travel more.", why:"〜さえ〜ば = 'if only…, (that's all it takes)'. しか needs a negative, and こそ can't go inside an if-clause like this."},
  {id:"p3-004", lv:"N3", ja:"まりやさんは[疲]{つか}れて、立つこと（　）できなかった。", ok:"さえ", opts:["さえ","こそ","ばかり","として"], en:"Mariya was so tired she couldn't even stand up.", why:"さえ + negative = 'couldn't even…'. こそ stresses something positive ('this one, above all'), so it clashes with できなかった."},
  {id:"p3-005", lv:"N3", ja:"A：どうもありがとうございました。B：こちら（　）、ありがとうございました。", ok:"こそ", opts:["こそ","さえ","でも","ばかり"], en:"A: Thank you very much. B: No, thank *you*.", why:"こちらこそ = 'I'm the one who should say it'. It's a set reply; さえ and でも would mean 'even me', which makes no sense here."},
  {id:"p3-006", lv:"N3", ja:"[今年]{ことし}（　）N3に[合格]{ごうかく}したい。", ok:"こそ", opts:["こそ","さえ","でも","ばかり"], en:"This year, for sure, I want to pass N3.", why:"こそ = 'this time for sure' (after failing before). [今年]{ことし}でも would mean 'even this year', and さえ needs a negative or an if-clause."},
  {id:"p3-007", lv:"N3", ja:"こんな時（　）、[落]{お}ち着いて考えよう。", ok:"こそ", opts:["こそ","さえ","ばかり","として"], en:"It's at times like this that we should stay calm and think.", why:"こそ picks out 'exactly this time'. さえ (even) doesn't fit a positive suggestion, and として means 'in the role of'."},
  {id:"p3-008", lv:"N3", ja:"すしやてんぷら（　）の[和食]{わしょく}は、外国でも人気がある。", ok:"など", opts:["など","ばかり","さえ","こそ"], en:"Japanese food such as sushi and tempura is popular abroad too.", why:"Aや Bなど = 'A, B and so on': など closes a list of examples. ばかり would mean 'nothing but'."},
  {id:"p3-009", lv:"N3", ja:"[忙]{いそが}しくて、テレビ（　）見ている時間はない。", ok:"なんか", opts:["なんか","こそ","として","によって"], en:"I'm so busy I have no time for things like watching TV.", why:"なんか (casual など) makes light of something: 'TV and that sort of thing'. こそ would stress TV as the most important thing."},
  {id:"p3-010", lv:"N3", ja:"そんな[難]{むずか}しい仕事、私（　）にはとてもできません。", ok:"など", opts:["など","こそ","さえ","でも"], en:"A difficult job like that is far beyond someone like me.", why:"私などには = 'someone like me' (humble). こそ, さえ and でも can't come before には in this way."},
  {id:"p3-011", lv:"N3", ja:"トビーさんは英語の先生（　）日本に来た。", ok:"として", opts:["として","にとって","について","に対して"], en:"Toby came to Japan as an English teacher.", why:"として = 'as, in the role of'. にとって = 'for, from the point of view of'; について = 'about'."},
  {id:"p3-012", lv:"N3", ja:"この[部屋]{へや}は今、[物置]{ものおき}（　）使っている。", ok:"として", opts:["として","にとって","について","によって"], en:"We use this room as a storeroom now.", why:"〜として使う = 'use as'. にとって is about who something matters to, not what it is used as."},
  {id:"p3-013", lv:"N3", ja:"私（　）は、それはいい考えだと思います。", ok:"として", opts:["として","について","によって","に対して"], en:"Speaking for myself, I think that's a good idea.", why:"私としては = 'for my part, speaking as me'. について (about) would make 'me' the subject of the idea."},
  {id:"p3-014", lv:"N3", ja:"私（　）、家族が[一番]{いちばん}大切です。", ok:"にとって", opts:["にとって","として","について","によって"], en:"For me, my family matters most.", why:"にとって = 'for, to (someone)': whose point of view. 私として would mean 'in my role as…', which needs a role."},
  {id:"p3-015", lv:"N3", ja:"この問題は日本人（　）も[難]{むずか}しい。", ok:"にとって", opts:["にとって","に対して","について","によって"], en:"This question is hard even for Japanese people.", why:"にとっても = 'even for'. に対して is about directing feelings or actions at someone, not about who finds something hard."},
  {id:"p3-016", lv:"N3", ja:"[若]{わか}い人（　）、スマホはなくてはならないものだ。", ok:"にとって", opts:["にとって","について","によって","として"], en:"For young people, a smartphone is something they can't do without.", why:"にとって gives the point of view: 'for young people'. について (about) and によって (depending on / by) don't fit."},
  {id:"p3-017", lv:"N3", ja:"チェスカさんは台風（　）研究している。", ok:"について", opts:["について","にとって","に対して","として"], en:"Cheska is researching typhoons.", why:"について = 'about, on (a topic)'. にとって (for) and として (as) don't mark the topic of research."},
  {id:"p3-018", lv:"N3", ja:"[会議]{かいぎ}では新しい計画（　）話し[合]{あ}った。", ok:"について", opts:["について","にとって","によって","に対して"], en:"At the meeting we discussed the new plan.", why:"Talking, thinking or writing *about* something takes について. に対して is for reacting or acting towards something."},
  {id:"p3-019", lv:"N3", ja:"この意見（　）、[反対]{はんたい}する人が多かった。", ok:"に対して", opts:["に対して","にとって","として","を通して"], en:"Many people were against this opinion.", why:"に対して = 'towards, against': the target of a reaction like [反対]{はんたい}する. にとって would mean 'for this opinion', as if it had a point of view."},
  {id:"p3-020", lv:"N3", ja:"目上の人（　）は、ていねいな[言葉]{ことば}を使いましょう。", ok:"に対して", opts:["に対して","にとって","を通して","にくらべて"], en:"Use polite language towards people above you.", why:"に対して marks who your words are aimed at. にとって is about whose point of view, which doesn't fit 'use polite language'."},
  {id:"p3-021", lv:"N3", ja:"人（　）考え方はちがう。", ok:"によって", opts:["によって","にとって","について","として"], en:"How people think differs from person to person.", why:"によって = 'depending on'. にとって (for) would need an evaluation, not ちがう."},
  {id:"p3-022", lv:"N3", ja:"この[絵]{え}はピカソ（　）かかれた。", ok:"によって", opts:["によって","にとって","に対して","として"], en:"This picture was painted by Picasso.", why:"In a passive about creating something, the maker takes によって. にとって, に対して and として can't mark who did it."},
  {id:"p3-023", lv:"N3", ja:"台風（　）、電車が止まった。", ok:"によって", opts:["によって","にとって","について","に対して"], en:"The trains stopped because of the typhoon.", why:"によって can give a cause in news-style Japanese (like で). にとって and について don't give causes."},
  {id:"p3-024", lv:"N3", ja:"[天気予報]{てんきよほう}（　）、[明日]{あした}は[雪]{ゆき}だそうだ。", ok:"によると", opts:["によると","によって","にとって","について"], en:"According to the weather forecast, it will snow tomorrow.", why:"によると = 'according to' a source, and it goes with そうだ or らしい. によって means 'depending on' or 'by'."},
  {id:"p3-025", lv:"N3", ja:"駅まで歩いて[十分]{じゅっぷん}（　）です。", ok:"くらい", opts:["くらい","しか","さえ","こそ"], en:"It's about ten minutes' walk to the station.", why:"くらい (ぐらい) = 'about' with an amount. しか needs a negative, and さえ/こそ add emphasis, not an estimate."},
  {id:"p3-026", lv:"N3", ja:"自分の[部屋]{へや}（　）自分でそうじしなさい。", ok:"くらい", opts:["くらい","ばかり","しか","として"], en:"At least clean your own room yourself.", why:"くらい can mean 'at least (this small thing)'. しか would need a negative; ばかり means 'nothing but'."},
  {id:"p3-027", lv:"N3", ja:"足が[痛]{いた}くて、もう歩けない（　）[疲]{つか}れた。", ok:"ほど", opts:["ほど","ばかり","さえ","こそ"], en:"My feet hurt; I'm so tired I can't walk any more.", why:"〜ほど = 'to the point that…' (degree). ばかり, さえ and こそ can't link a clause to an adjective like this."},
  {id:"p3-028", lv:"N3", ja:"日本語は勉強すればする（　）、おもしろくなる。", ok:"ほど", opts:["ほど","くらい","ばかり","さえ"], en:"The more you study Japanese, the more interesting it gets.", why:"〜ば〜ほど = 'the more…, the more…'. It is a fixed pattern; くらい can't replace ほど here."},
  {id:"p3-029", lv:"N3", ja:"雨だけでなく、風（　）強くなってきた。", ok:"まで", opts:["まで","こそ","ほど","として"], en:"Not only the rain: now even the wind has picked up.", why:"まで = 'even (on top of everything)'. こそ singles out something good or important, and ほど gives a degree."},
  {id:"p3-030", lv:"N3", ja:"[疲]{つか}れたね。お茶（　）飲みませんか。", ok:"でも", opts:["でも","さえ","こそ","しか"], en:"I'm tired. How about a cup of tea or something?", why:"Noun + でも in an invitation = 'or something' (softens it). さえ and こそ add strong emphasis, and しか needs a negative."},
  {id:"p3-031", lv:"N3", ja:"そんなことは子ども（　）知っているよ。", ok:"でも", opts:["でも","こそ","しか","として"], en:"Even a child knows that.", why:"でも = 'even'. こそ would say a child is *the* one who knows, and として would mean 'as a child'."},
  {id:"p3-032", lv:"N3", ja:"この[薬]{くすり}は一日に[一回]{いっかい}（　）飲んではいけません。", ok:"しか", opts:["しか","ばかり","さえ","こそ"], en:"You may only take this medicine once a day.", why:"しか + negative = 'only': once and no more. ばかり means 'nothing but', and こそ would stress 'once' as the best."},
  {id:"p3-033", lv:"N3", ja:"日本に来た（　）なので、まだ何もわかりません。", ok:"ばかり", opts:["ばかり","しか","ほど","さえ"], en:"I've only just arrived in Japan, so I don't know anything yet.", why:"た-form + ばかり = 'have just done'. しか and ほど can't follow a past verb to mean 'just'."},
  {id:"p3-034", lv:"N3", ja:"あの店は安い（　）でなく、味もいい。", ok:"だけ", opts:["だけ","しか","ほど","さえ"], en:"That shop isn't just cheap; the food tastes good too.", why:"〜だけでなく = 'not only'. しかでなく is not a pattern; ほど and さえ don't fit before でなく."},
  {id:"p3-035", lv:"N3", ja:"[昨日]{きのう}私（　）会った人は、ロドリゴさんの先生だった。", ok:"が", opts:["が","は","を","で"], en:"The person I met yesterday was Rodrigo's teacher.", why:"Inside a clause describing a noun (〜会った人), the subject takes が, not は. 会う takes に for the person met, so を is wrong too."},
  {id:"p3-036", lv:"N3", ja:"去年（　）、[今年]{ことし}は[雪]{ゆき}が少ない。", ok:"にくらべて", opts:["にくらべて","について","によって","にとって"], en:"Compared with last year, there's little snow this year.", why:"〜にくらべて = 'compared with'. について (about), によって (depending on) and にとって (for) don't compare."},
  {id:"p3-037", lv:"N3", ja:"この[箱]{はこ}は本を入れる（　）ちょうどいい。", ok:"のに", opts:["のに","けど","ほど","さえ"], en:"This box is just right for putting books in.", why:"Verb + のに + ちょうどいい / [便利]{べんり} = 'for (doing)'. けど (but) would leave the sentence without a link."},
  {id:"p3-038", lv:"N3", ja:"あおいさんとは友だち（　）知り[合]{あ}った。", ok:"を通して", opts:["を通して","について","にとって","に対して"], en:"I got to know Aoi through a friend.", why:"〜を通して = 'through (someone or something)'. について (about) and にとって (for) don't say how you met."},
  {id:"p3-039", lv:"N3", ja:"[初]{はじ}めて作った（　）、このケーキはおいしいね。", ok:"にしては", opts:["にしては","にとって","について","によって"], en:"For a first try, this cake is good!", why:"〜にしては = 'considering, for (something you'd expect less from)'. にとって (for a person) and について (about) don't give that 'better than expected' feeling."},
  {id:"p3-040", lv:"N3", ja:"さっき、山口さん（　）人から電話があったよ。", ok:"って", opts:["って","とか","こそ","さえ"], en:"A little while ago, someone called Yamaguchi phoned you.", why:"Name + って + 人 = 'someone called…' (casual という). とか lists examples, and こそ/さえ add emphasis."}
],
builder: [
  {id:"b5-001", lv:"N5", tiles:["わたしは","[毎日]{まいにち}","[日本語]{にほんご}を","べんきょうします"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"I study Japanese every day.", why:"The verb goes last. A time word like [毎日]{まいにち} can go before or after わたしは, or just before the verb."},
  {id:"b5-002", lv:"N5", tiles:["これは","まりやさんの","かさ","です"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"This is Mariya's umbrella.", why:"XはYです: topic first, です last. まりやさんの must sit right before the noun it describes."},
  {id:"b5-003", lv:"N5", tiles:["[学校]{がっこう}の","[前]{まえ}に","コンビニが","あります"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[2,0,1,3]], en:"There's a convenience store in front of the school.", why:"Place に, thing が, あります. 'Place first' is the usual order, but the thing can come first too. [学校]{がっこう}の stays before [前]{まえ}に."},
  {id:"b5-004", lv:"N5", tiles:["ロドリゴさんは","バスで","[学校]{がっこう}へ","[行]{い}きます"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"Rodrigo goes to school by bus.", why:"Topic first, verb last. バスで and [学校]{がっこう}へ can swap places."},
  {id:"b5-005", lv:"N5", tiles:["[父]{ちち}は","[高校]{こうこう}で","えいごを","おしえています"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"My father teaches English at a high school.", why:"The place (で) and the object (を) can swap, but the verb stays last."},
  {id:"b5-006", lv:"N5", tiles:["[日本]{にほん}の","[山]{やま}は","とても","きれいです"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"Japan's mountains are very beautiful.", why:"[日本]{にほん}の describes [山]{やま}, so it comes right before it. とても goes right before the word it strengthens."},
  {id:"b5-007", lv:"N5", tiles:["ここで","しゃしんを","とっても","いいですか"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3]], en:"May I take photos here?", why:"〜てもいいですか ends the sentence. ここで and しゃしんを can swap."},
  {id:"b5-008", lv:"N5", tiles:["すみません、","もういちど","ゆっくり","いってください"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"Excuse me, could you say that again slowly?", why:"すみません opens the request and 〜てください closes it. もういちど and ゆっくり can swap."},
  {id:"b5-009", lv:"N5", tiles:["わたしは","あたたかい","コーヒーが","のみたいです"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"I'd like to drink some hot coffee.", why:"An adjective goes right before its noun: あたたかいコーヒー. The verb (〜たいです) is last."},
  {id:"b5-010", lv:"N5", tiles:["[今]{いま}","[外]{そと}は","[雨]{あめ}が","ふっています"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3]], en:"It's raining outside right now.", why:"[今]{いま} can go before or after [外]{そと}は. [雨]{あめ}が goes with the verb at the end."},
  {id:"b5-011", lv:"N5", tiles:["この[本]{ほん}は","あの[本]{ほん}より","おもしろいです"], orders:[[0,1,2]], en:"This book is more interesting than that one.", why:"XはYより〜: the topic (X) first, then 'than Y', then the adjective."},
  {id:"b5-012", lv:"N5", tiles:["[電車]{でんしゃ}と","バスと","どちらが","はやいですか"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3]], en:"Which is faster, the train or the bus?", why:"AとBと、どちらが〜ですか. The two choices can come in either order."},
  {id:"b5-013", lv:"N5", tiles:["わたしは","[毎日]{まいにち}","[七時]{しちじ}に","おきます"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3]], en:"I get up at seven every day.", why:"The general time ([毎日]{まいにち}) comes before the exact time ([七時]{しちじ}に). わたしは can go first or second."},
  {id:"b5-014", lv:"N5", tiles:["[日本]{にほん}の","[食]{た}べものの","[中]{なか}で","[何]{なに}が","いちばんすきですか"], orders:[[0,1,2,3,4]], en:"Of all Japanese foods, which do you like best?", why:"〜の[中]{なか}で sets the group, then the question word with が, then いちばん + adjective."},
  {id:"b5-015", lv:"N5", tiles:["[母]{はは}に","[電話]{でんわ}を","かけました"], orders:[[0,1,2],[1,0,2]], en:"I called my mother.", why:"The verb is last; the person (に) and the object (を) can swap."},
  {id:"b5-016", lv:"N5", tiles:["まりやさんは","[今]{いま}","へやで","ねています"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"Mariya is sleeping in her room right now.", why:"The verb is last. [今]{いま} can go before or after the topic, or just before the verb."},
  {id:"b5-017", lv:"N5", tiles:["このへやで","たばこを","すわないでください"], orders:[[0,1,2],[1,0,2]], en:"Please don't smoke in this room.", why:"〜ないでください ends the sentence. The place and the object can swap."},
  {id:"b5-018", lv:"N5", tiles:["イエンさんは","[日本]{にほん}の","かいしゃで","[四年間]{よねんかん}","はたらきました"], orders:[[0,1,2,3,4],[0,3,1,2,4]], en:"Yến worked at a Japanese company for four years.", why:"[日本]{にほん}の must stay right before かいしゃ. The length of time can go before the verb or before the place."},
  {id:"b5-019", lv:"N5", tiles:["つくえの","[上]{うえ}に","[本]{ほん}が","[三]{さん}さつ","あります"], orders:[[0,1,2,3,4],[2,3,0,1,4],[2,0,1,3,4]], en:"There are three books on the desk.", why:"The counter usually follows its noun ([本]{ほん}が[三]{さん}さつ). The place can come first or after the thing."},
  {id:"b5-020", lv:"N5", tiles:["わたしは","きのう","どこへも","[行]{い}きませんでした"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3]], en:"I didn't go anywhere yesterday.", why:"きのう can go before or after わたしは. どこへも goes with the negative verb at the end."},
  {id:"b5-021", lv:"N5", tiles:["あした","いっしょに","ひるごはんを","[食]{た}べませんか"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"Would you like to have lunch together tomorrow?", why:"Time first, the invitation (〜ませんか) last. いっしょに can go before or after the object."},
  {id:"b5-022", lv:"N5", tiles:["[雨]{あめ}ですから","タクシーで","[行]{い}きましょう"], orders:[[0,1,2]], en:"It's raining, so let's take a taxi.", why:"The reason (〜から) comes first, then what to do."},
  {id:"b5-023", lv:"N5", tiles:["あの","せが[高]{たか}い","[人]{ひと}は","だれですか"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3]], en:"Who is that tall person?", why:"Both あの and せが[高]{たか}い describe [人]{ひと}, so both go before it, in either order."},
  {id:"b5-024", lv:"N5", tiles:["[白]{しろ}い","シャツを","[二]{に}まい","ください"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"Two white shirts, please.", why:"Adjective before noun; the number + counter goes after the noun and its particle."},
  {id:"b5-025", lv:"N5", tiles:["すみません、","[水]{みず}を","[一]{いっ}ぱい","ください"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"Excuse me, a glass of water, please.", why:"Noun を + number + ください is the usual way to order."},
  {id:"b5-026", lv:"N5", tiles:["チェスカさんは","[大学]{だいがく}で","[日本語]{にほんご}を","ならっています"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"Cheska is learning Japanese at the university.", why:"The place (で) and the object (を) can swap; the verb stays last."},
  {id:"b5-027", lv:"N5", tiles:["わたしの","へやは","ひろくて","あかるいです"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"My room is big and bright.", why:"The て-form (ひろくて) links to the next adjective, so it comes first; the polite ending です is last."},
  {id:"b5-028", lv:"N5", tiles:["ここは","あぶないですから","[川]{かわ}で","およがないでください"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"It's dangerous here, so please don't swim in the river.", why:"Reason clause first (ここはあぶないですから), then the request."},
  {id:"b5-029", lv:"N5", tiles:["ここに","[名前]{なまえ}を","[書]{か}いてください"], orders:[[0,1,2],[1,0,2]], en:"Please write your name here.", why:"The place (に) and the object (を) can swap before the verb."},
  {id:"b5-030", lv:"N5", tiles:["トビーさんは","[日本語]{にほんご}が","とても","じょうずです"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"Toby is very good at Japanese.", why:"XはYがじょうずです. とても usually sits right before じょうず, but it can also come before [日本語]{にほんご}が."},
  {id:"b5-031", lv:"N5", tiles:["きのうは","あまり","[天気]{てんき}が","よくなかったです"], orders:[[0,2,1,3],[0,1,2,3]], en:"The weather wasn't very good yesterday.", why:"あまり + negative: it most naturally sits right before よくなかった, but it can also come before [天気]{てんき}が."},
  {id:"b5-032", lv:"N5", tiles:["うちには","ねこが","[二]{に}ひき","います"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"We have two cats at home.", why:"Place には, then the animal が + number + counter, then います."},
  {id:"b5-033", lv:"N5", tiles:["[毎日]{まいにち}","[何時]{なんじ}に","[学校]{がっこう}へ","[行]{い}きますか"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"What time do you go to school every day?", why:"General time first. [何時]{なんじ}に and [学校]{がっこう}へ can swap."},
  {id:"b5-034", lv:"N5", tiles:["あしたは","[休]{やす}みですから","うちで","ゆっくりします"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"Tomorrow is my day off, so I'll take it easy at home.", why:"The reason (あしたは[休]{やす}みですから) comes first, then the plan."},
  {id:"b5-035", lv:"N5", tiles:["もうすこし","[大]{おお}きい","こえで","[話]{はな}してください"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"Please speak a little louder.", why:"もうすこし modifies [大]{おお}きい, which modifies こえ, so they stay in this order."},
  {id:"b5-036", lv:"N5", tiles:["わたしは","ねこより","いぬのほうが","すきです"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"I like dogs more than cats.", why:"〜より and 〜のほうが can swap; すきです stays last."},
  {id:"b5-037", lv:"N5", tiles:["かいとさんは","としょかんで","しゅくだいを","しています"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"Kaito is doing his homework at the library.", why:"The place and the object can swap; the verb stays last."},
  {id:"b5-038", lv:"N5", tiles:["つぎのかどを","[左]{ひだり}に","まがってください"], orders:[[0,1,2]], en:"Please turn left at the next corner.", why:"The corner (を) comes first, then the direction (に), then the verb."},
  {id:"b5-039", lv:"N5", tiles:["ロドリゴさんは","[毎日]{まいにち}","こうえんで","えを","かいています"], orders:[[0,1,2,3,4],[1,0,2,3,4],[0,2,1,3,4]], en:"Rodrigo draws pictures in the park every day.", why:"えを stays next to the verb. [毎日]{まいにち} and こうえんで can move around the topic."},
  {id:"b5-040", lv:"N5", tiles:["[百円]{ひゃくえん}の","りんごを","[五]{いつ}つ","かいました"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"I bought five 100-yen apples.", why:"[百円]{ひゃくえん}の describes りんご; the number comes after りんごを."},
  {id:"b5-041", lv:"N5", tiles:["きのう","[友]{とも}だちと","えいがを","[見]{み}ました"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"Yesterday I watched a movie with a friend.", why:"Time first. [友]{とも}だちと and えいがを can swap."},
  {id:"b5-042", lv:"N5", tiles:["しゅくだいを","してから","テレビを","[見]{み}ます"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"I'll watch TV after I do my homework.", why:"〜てから: the first action comes first. Swapping the objects would make nonsense."},
  {id:"b5-043", lv:"N5", tiles:["[外]{そと}は","さむいですから","コートを","きて","[行]{い}きましょう"], orders:[[0,1,2,3,4]], en:"It's cold outside, so let's wear coats.", why:"Reason first; コートをきて (wearing a coat) comes before the main verb."},
  {id:"b5-044", lv:"N5", tiles:["まりやさんの","お[母]{かあ}さんは","しおじまに","すんでいます"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"Mariya's mother lives on Shiojima.", why:"まりやさんの describes お[母]{かあ}さん; place に before すんでいます."},
  {id:"b5-045", lv:"N5", tiles:["トビーさんは","いつも","[何時]{なんじ}ごろ","ねますか"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"About what time does Toby usually go to bed?", why:"Topic, then いつも, then the question word and the verb."},
  {id:"b5-046", lv:"N5", tiles:["このケーキ、","[一]{ひと}つ","[食]{た}べても","いいですか"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"May I have one of these cakes?", why:"The thing first, then the number, then 〜てもいいですか."},
  {id:"b5-047", lv:"N5", tiles:["[学校]{がっこう}は","[九時]{くじ}から","[三時]{さんじ}まで","です"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"School is from nine to three.", why:"から comes before まで, and です ends the sentence."},
  {id:"b5-048", lv:"N5", tiles:["[来月]{らいげつ}","[友]{とも}だちが","[国]{くに}から","[来]{き}ます"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3],[0,2,1,3],[1,2,0,3]], en:"Next month a friend is coming from my home country.", why:"The verb is last; the time, the person and 'from my country' can move around before it."},
  {id:"b5-049", lv:"N5", tiles:["[何]{なに}か","つめたい","のみものは","ありますか"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,2,0,3]], en:"Do you have something cold to drink?", why:"つめたい stays before のみもの. [何]{なに}か can go first or just before the verb."},
  {id:"b5-050", lv:"N5", tiles:["わたしは","まだ","[日本語]{にほんご}が","よく","わかりません"], orders:[[0,1,2,3,4],[0,2,1,3,4]], en:"I still don't understand Japanese very well.", why:"よく goes right before the verb. まだ can come before or after [日本語]{にほんご}が."},
  {id:"b4-001", lv:"N4", tiles:["これは","母が","[作]{つく}った","ケーキです"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"This is a cake my mother made.", why:"A describing clause (母が[作]{つく}った) goes right before its noun, like an adjective."},
  {id:"b4-002", lv:"N4", tiles:["[駅]{えき}で","[買]{か}った","本を","きのう","読みました"], orders:[[3,0,1,2,4],[0,1,2,3,4]], en:"Yesterday I read the book I bought at the station.", why:"[駅]{えき}で[買]{か}った describes 本, so the three stay together in that order. きのう can go first or just before the verb."},
  {id:"b4-003", lv:"N4", tiles:["雨がふったら","あしたの","しあいは","[中止]{ちゅうし}です"], orders:[[1,2,0,3],[0,1,2,3]], en:"If it rains, tomorrow's match will be called off.", why:"The topic (あしたのしあいは) and the 〜たら clause can swap. あしたの stays before しあい."},
  {id:"b4-004", lv:"N4", tiles:["先生に","聞けば","すぐ","わかりますよ"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"If you ask the teacher, you'll understand right away.", why:"The 〜ば clause (先生に聞けば) comes first; すぐ goes right before the verb it describes."},
  {id:"b4-005", lv:"N4", tiles:["まりやさんが","[私]{わたし}に","[地図]{ちず}を","かいてくれました"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"Mariya drew me a map.", why:"With 〜てくれる the giver is the subject. The receiver (に) and the object (を) can swap."},
  {id:"b4-006", lv:"N4", tiles:["[弟]{おとうと}に","[自転車]{じてんしゃ}を","[貸]{か}して","あげました"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3]], en:"I lent my bike to my little brother.", why:"〜てあげました ends the sentence. The person (に) and the thing (を) can swap."},
  {id:"b4-007", lv:"N4", tiles:["[旅行]{りょこう}に行く前に","ガイドブックを","[買]{か}って","おきます"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3]], en:"I'll buy a guidebook before I go on the trip.", why:"〜ておきます (do in advance) stays last. The 'before' clause and the object can swap."},
  {id:"b4-008", lv:"N4", tiles:["[大切]{たいせつ}な","本を","電車に","わすれてしまいました"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[2,0,1,3]], en:"I left an important book on the train.", why:"[大切]{たいせつ}な must stay right before 本. 電車に can go before or after that phrase."},
  {id:"b4-009", lv:"N4", tiles:["日本に来てから","毎日","にっきを","書いています"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"Since coming to Japan, I've been keeping a diary every day.", why:"The 〜てから clause sets the time frame, so it comes first. 毎日 and にっきを can swap."},
  {id:"b4-010", lv:"N4", tiles:["この[道]{みち}を","まっすぐ行くと","左に","[駅]{えき}が","あります"], orders:[[0,1,2,3,4],[0,1,3,2,4]], en:"If you go straight along this road, the station is on the left.", why:"The と clause comes first. After it, 左に and [駅]{えき}が can swap."},
  {id:"b4-011", lv:"N4", tiles:["[兄]{あに}は","[漢字]{かんじ}が","読めるのに","書けません"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"My older brother can read kanji, but he can't write them.", why:"〜のに (even though) joins the two verbs: can read, yet can't write. The topic and what he reads come first."},
  {id:"b4-012", lv:"N4", tiles:["子どもの時","母に","やさいを","食べさせられました"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"When I was a child, my mother made me eat vegetables.", why:"Time first; the causative-passive verb last. 母に and やさいを can swap."},
  {id:"b4-013", lv:"N4", tiles:["先生に","[作文]{さくぶん}を","なおしてもらいました"], orders:[[0,1,2],[1,0,2]], en:"I had my teacher correct my essay.", why:"〜てもらう: the helper (に) and the object (を) can swap before the verb."},
  {id:"b4-014", lv:"N4", tiles:["あしたは","[早]{はや}く","[起]{お}きなければ","なりません"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"I have to get up early tomorrow.", why:"〜なければなりません is split over two tiles and stays in that order; [早]{はや}く goes before the verb it describes."},
  {id:"b4-015", lv:"N4", tiles:["だれもいないのに","[教室]{きょうしつ}の","ドアが","[開]{あ}いています"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,2,0,3]], en:"The classroom door is open, even though nobody is there.", why:"The のに clause usually comes first, but it can also follow [教室]{きょうしつ}のドアが. [教室]{きょうしつ}の stays before ドア; intransitive [開]{あ}いています is last."},
  {id:"b4-016", lv:"N4", tiles:["[黒]{くろ}い","めがねを","かけている","人が","[兄]{あに}です"], orders:[[0,1,2,3,4]], en:"The person wearing black glasses is my older brother.", why:"Everything before 人 describes him: [黒]{くろ}いめがねをかけている人. Then が and [兄]{あに}です."},
  {id:"b4-017", lv:"N4", tiles:["[音楽]{おんがく}を","聞きながら","[勉強]{べんきょう}するのは","よくないですよ"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"Studying while listening to music isn't a good idea.", why:"〜ながら: the side action comes first, then the main one. 〜のは turns it into the topic."},
  {id:"b4-018", lv:"N4", tiles:["この[町]{まち}は","しずかだし","[空気]{くうき}も","きれいだ"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"This town is quiet, and the air is clean too.", why:"〜し lists reasons; the clause with し comes first and the last one ends the sentence."},
  {id:"b4-019", lv:"N4", tiles:["あした","雨が","ふるかどうか","まだ","わかりません"], orders:[[0,1,2,3,4],[3,0,1,2,4]], en:"I don't know yet whether it will rain tomorrow.", why:"The かどうか clause stays together (あした雨がふるかどうか). まだ goes before the clause or right before the verb."},
  {id:"b4-020", lv:"N4", tiles:["[夏休]{なつやす}みに","[海]{うみ}へ","行こうと","[思]{おも}っています"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3]], en:"I'm thinking of going to the beach in the summer holidays.", why:"Volitional + と[思]{おも}っています ends it. The time and the place can swap."},
  {id:"b4-021", lv:"N4", tiles:["電車の中で","[知]{し}らない人に","話しかけられました"], orders:[[0,1,2],[1,0,2]], en:"A stranger started talking to me on the train.", why:"Passive verb last; the place and the doer (に) can swap."},
  {id:"b4-022", lv:"N4", tiles:["この[服]{ふく}は","小さすぎて","もう","[着]{き}られません"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"These clothes are too small, so I can't wear them any more.", why:"もう can go right before the verb or before 小さすぎて."},
  {id:"b4-023", lv:"N4", tiles:["ここに","車を","[止]{と}めないで","ください"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3]], en:"Please don't park your car here.", why:"〜ないでください ends it. The place and the object can swap."},
  {id:"b4-024", lv:"N4", tiles:["天気がよければ","あした","山に","のぼりましょう"], orders:[[1,0,2,3],[0,1,2,3]], en:"If the weather's good, let's climb the mountain tomorrow.", why:"あした can come before or after the 〜ば clause. 山に stays next to the verb."},
  {id:"b4-025", lv:"N4", tiles:["[兄]{あに}は","[私]{わたし}より","三つ","年上です"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"My older brother is three years older than me.", why:"Topic, then 〜より, then the amount right before 年上."},
  {id:"b4-026", lv:"N4", tiles:["まりやさんは","[料理]{りょうり}が","[上手]{じょうず}だと","[思]{おも}います"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"I think Mariya is a good cook.", why:"The quoted thought (〜だと) comes before [思]{おも}います."},
  {id:"b4-027", lv:"N4", tiles:["日本の","せいかつに","もう","なれましたか"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[2,0,1,3]], en:"Have you got used to life in Japan yet?", why:"日本の stays before せいかつ. もう can go first or right before the verb."},
  {id:"b4-028", lv:"N4", tiles:["[字]{じ}が","小さくて","よく","見えません"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"The writing is so small I can't see it well.", why:"The reason (〜くて) first; よく goes right before the verb."},
  {id:"b4-029", lv:"N4", tiles:["もし","一万円あったら","何を","[買]{か}いますか"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"If you had 10,000 yen, what would you buy?", why:"もし opens the 〜たら clause; the question comes after it."},
  {id:"b4-030", lv:"N4", tiles:["[姉]{あね}は","[毎朝]{まいあさ}","ジョギングを","しているらしい"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3]], en:"Apparently my older sister goes jogging every morning.", why:"〜らしい ends it. [毎朝]{まいあさ} can come before or after the topic."},
  {id:"b4-031", lv:"N4", tiles:["あの[店]{みせ}の","ラーメンは","[安]{やす}くて","おいしいそうです"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"I hear the ramen at that shop is cheap and tasty.", why:"あの[店]{みせ}の describes ラーメン; 〜くて links the two adjectives before そうです."},
  {id:"b4-032", lv:"N4", tiles:["食べる前に","[手]{て}を","あらって","ください"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"Please wash your hands before eating.", why:"The 'before' clause first, then the request."},
  {id:"b4-033", lv:"N4", tiles:["[試験]{しけん}が[終]{お}わったら","いっしょに","カラオケに","行きましょう"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"When the exam is over, let's go to karaoke together.", why:"The 〜たら clause first. いっしょに and カラオケに can swap."},
  {id:"b4-034", lv:"N4", tiles:["父に","[写真]{しゃしん}を","見せて","もらいました"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3]], en:"My father showed me some photos.", why:"〜てもらいました ends it; the person (に) and the object (を) can swap."},
  {id:"b4-035", lv:"N4", tiles:["[医者]{いしゃ}に","たばこを","やめるように","[言]{い}われました"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,2,0,3]], en:"My doctor told me to stop smoking.", why:"たばこをやめるように stays together. [医者]{いしゃ}に can go before or after it."},
  {id:"b4-036", lv:"N4", tiles:["[妹]{いもうと}が","生まれた","時","[私]{わたし}は","五さいでした"], orders:[[0,1,2,3,4],[3,0,1,2,4]], en:"When my little sister was born, I was five.", why:"[妹]{いもうと}が生まれた時 stays together; [私]{わたし}は can go before or after it."},
  {id:"b4-037", lv:"N4", tiles:["[急]{いそ}がないと","電車に","まにあいませんよ"], orders:[[0,1,2]], en:"If you don't hurry, you'll miss the train.", why:"The と clause (condition) comes first, then the result."},
  {id:"b4-038", lv:"N4", tiles:["友だちに","[借]{か}りた","本を","かえさなきゃ"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"I've got to return the book I borrowed from my friend.", why:"友だちに[借]{か}りた describes 本, so it comes right before it. Casual 〜なきゃ ends the sentence."},
  {id:"b4-039", lv:"N4", tiles:["[昼]{ひる}ご[飯]{はん}を","食べた","あとで","コーヒーを[飲]{の}みました"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"After eating lunch, I had a coffee.", why:"〜たあとで: the first action, then あとで, then the second."},
  {id:"b4-040", lv:"N4", tiles:["[海]{うみ}が","見える","へやを","よやくしました"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"I booked a room with a sea view.", why:"[海]{うみ}が見える describes へや, so it comes right before it."},
  {id:"b4-041", lv:"N4", tiles:["父は","[歌]{うた}が","[下手]{へた}なのに","よくカラオケに行きます"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"My dad often goes to karaoke, even though he's a bad singer.", why:"The のに clause comes first, then the surprising fact."},
  {id:"b4-042", lv:"N4", tiles:["[家]{いえ}に","[着]{つ}いたら","電話を","ください"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"Please call me when you get home.", why:"The 〜たら clause ([家]{いえ}に[着]{つ}いたら) first, then the request."},
  {id:"b4-043", lv:"N4", tiles:["[姉]{あね}は","車の","[運転]{うんてん}が","[上手]{じょうず}です"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"My older sister is a good driver.", why:"車の describes [運転]{うんてん}; XはYが[上手]{じょうず}です."},
  {id:"b4-044", lv:"N4", tiles:["[犬]{いぬ}に","[手]{て}を","かまれました"], orders:[[0,1,2],[1,0,2]], en:"I got bitten on the hand by a dog.", why:"Passive verb last; the doer (に) and the body part (を) can swap."},
  {id:"b4-045", lv:"N4", tiles:["その[重]{おも}い","かばん、","[持]{も}って","あげましょうか"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"Shall I carry that heavy bag for you?", why:"その[重]{おも}い describes かばん; 〜てあげましょうか offers help at the end."},
  {id:"b4-046", lv:"N4", tiles:["[今度]{こんど}の[日曜日]{にちようび}","いっしょに","[映画]{えいが}を","見に行きませんか"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"Would you like to go and see a movie together this Sunday?", why:"Time first; いっしょに and [映画]{えいが}を can swap."},
  {id:"b4-047", lv:"N4", tiles:["[春]{はる}と","[秋]{あき}と","どちらのほうが","すきですか"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3]], en:"Which do you like better, spring or autumn?", why:"AとBと、どちらのほうが: the two choices can come in either order."},
  {id:"b4-048", lv:"N4", tiles:["この[漢字]{かんじ}の","読み[方]{かた}を","[教]{おし}えて","くれませんか"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"Could you tell me how to read this kanji?", why:"この[漢字]{かんじ}の describes 読み[方]{かた}; 〜てくれませんか ends the request."},
  {id:"b4-049", lv:"N4", tiles:["わからないことばが","あったら","先生に","聞いてください"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"If there are words you don't know, ask the teacher.", why:"The 〜たら clause first, then the instruction."},
  {id:"b4-050", lv:"N4", tiles:["[朝]{あさ}から","何も","食べていないので","おなかがすきました"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3]], en:"I haven't eaten anything since this morning, so I'm hungry.", why:"The ので clause first. [朝]{あさ}から and 何も can swap."},
  {id:"b3-001", lv:"N3", tiles:["日本語が","[上手]{じょうず}に","話せるように","毎日","れんしゅうしている"], orders:[[0,1,2,3,4],[3,0,1,2,4]], en:"I practise every day so that I can speak Japanese well.", why:"The purpose clause (〜ように) stays together and comes before the verb. 毎日 can go first or just before the verb."},
  {id:"b3-002", lv:"N3", tiles:["[太]{ふと}らないように","夜は","あまり","食べないようにしている"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3]], en:"So I don't put on weight, I try not to eat much at night.", why:"あまり goes right before the negative verb. The purpose clause and 夜は can swap."},
  {id:"b3-003", lv:"N3", tiles:["来月から","東京の","本社で","[働]{はたら}くことになった"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,2,0,3]], en:"It's been decided that I'll work at the Tokyo head office from next month.", why:"東京の stays before 本社. The time and the place can swap; 〜ことになった is last."},
  {id:"b3-004", lv:"N3", tiles:["今","出かける","ところなので","後で","電話するね"], orders:[[0,1,2,3,4]], en:"I'm just about to go out, so I'll call you later.", why:"今 + dictionary form + ところ = 'just about to'. The reason (〜ので) comes before the main clause."},
  {id:"b3-005", lv:"N3", tiles:["[会議]{かいぎ}は","もう","始まっている","はずだ"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"The meeting should have started already.", why:"はずだ follows the plain verb at the end; もう goes before the verb."},
  {id:"b3-006", lv:"N3", tiles:["あんなに","勉強したのだから","[合格]{ごうかく}する","はずだ"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"After studying that hard, you're bound to pass.", why:"あんなに describes 勉強した, so it comes first; the reason clause comes before 〜はずだ."},
  {id:"b3-007", lv:"N3", tiles:["子どもには","自分の","[好]{す}きな","道を","[選]{えら}んでほしい"], orders:[[0,1,2,3,4]], en:"I want my children to choose the path they love.", why:"自分の[好]{す}きな describes 道 and stays before it. 〜てほしい ends the sentence."},
  {id:"b3-008", lv:"N3", tiles:["友だちが[手伝]{てつだ}ってくれた","おかげで","[引]{ひ}っ[越]{こ}しが","早く終わった"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"Thanks to my friends helping, the move was over quickly.", why:"〜おかげで follows the clause it explains; the result comes after."},
  {id:"b3-009", lv:"N3", tiles:["雨の","せいで","[試合]{しあい}が","中止になった"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"The match was called off because of the rain.", why:"Noun + の + せいで gives a cause (for something bad); the result follows."},
  {id:"b3-010", lv:"N3", tiles:["考えれば","考えるほど","わからなく","なる"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"The more I think about it, the less I understand.", why:"〜ば〜ほど: the ば form comes first, then the same verb + ほど."},
  {id:"b3-011", lv:"N3", tiles:["この問題について","[皆]{みな}さんの","意見を","聞かせてください"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"Please tell me what you all think about this issue.", why:"The topic phrase (〜について) comes first; [皆]{みな}さんの describes 意見."},
  {id:"b3-012", lv:"N3", tiles:["[留学生]{りゅうがくせい}にとって","日本で","アパートを","[探]{さが}すのは","[大変]{たいへん}だ"], orders:[[0,1,2,3,4],[1,2,3,0,4]], en:"For international students, finding a flat in Japan is hard.", why:"日本でアパートを[探]{さが}すのは stays together. 〜にとって can go first or just before [大変]{たいへん}だ."},
  {id:"b3-013", lv:"N3", tiles:["チェスカさんは","台風の","研究を","するために","日本に来た"], orders:[[0,1,2,3,4]], en:"Cheska came to Japan to do research on typhoons.", why:"台風の研究をするために is one purpose clause; it comes before the main verb."},
  {id:"b3-014", lv:"N3", tiles:["日本にいる","うちに","一度","ふじさんに[登]{のぼ}りたい"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"While I'm in Japan, I want to climb Mt Fuji at least once.", why:"〜うちに follows its clause (日本にいる). 一度 goes right before what you want to do."},
  {id:"b3-015", lv:"N3", tiles:["母が料理をしている","間に","[部屋]{へや}を","かたづけた"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"While my mother was cooking, I tidied my room.", why:"〜間に follows its clause; then the action done during that time."},
  {id:"b3-016", lv:"N3", tiles:["この写真を","見る","たびに","国の家族を思い出す"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"Every time I look at this photo, I think of my family back home.", why:"Dictionary form + たびに = 'every time'; the clause stays in order before the result."},
  {id:"b3-017", lv:"N3", tiles:["料理を作ってもらう","かわりに","私が","[洗]{あら}い物をする"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"In return for having the cooking done for me, I do the washing-up.", why:"〜かわりに follows its clause; then what you do in return."},
  {id:"b3-018", lv:"N3", tiles:["この町は","東京にくらべて","ぶっかが","安い"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3]], en:"Compared with Tokyo, prices in this town are low.", why:"The topic and the 〜にくらべて phrase can swap. ぶっかが stays with 安い."},
  {id:"b3-019", lv:"N3", tiles:["肉が","食べられない","わけではないが","あまり[好]{す}きではない"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"It's not that I can't eat meat, but I don't really like it.", why:"〜わけではないが denies the clause before it, then the real point follows."},
  {id:"b3-020", lv:"N3", tiles:["まだ時間があるから","そんなに","急ぐ","ことはない"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"We still have time, so there's no need to rush like that.", why:"Reason first; そんなに describes 急ぐ; 〜ことはない ends it."},
  {id:"b3-021", lv:"N3", tiles:["子どものころは","よく","この川で","[泳]{およ}いだものだ"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"When I was a child, I often used to swim in this river.", why:"〜ものだ (used to) ends it. よく and この川で can swap."},
  {id:"b3-022", lv:"N3", tiles:["[明日]{あした}の","[会議]{かいぎ}って","何時から","だっけ"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"What time does tomorrow's meeting start again?", why:"[明日]{あした}の describes [会議]{かいぎ}; って marks the topic in casual speech; だっけ checks something you've forgotten."},
  {id:"b3-023", lv:"N3", tiles:["[最近]{さいきん}","かぜ[気味]{ぎみ}で","[頭]{あたま}が","[痛]{いた}い"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"I've had a bit of a cold lately and my head hurts.", why:"Time first; the cause (〜[気味]{ぎみ}で) before the result."},
  {id:"b3-024", lv:"N3", tiles:["兄は","[忘]{わす}れっぽくて","よくかさを","なくす"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"My brother is forgetful and often loses his umbrella.", why:"〜っぽくて gives the trait, then what happens because of it."},
  {id:"b3-025", lv:"N3", tiles:["[寒]{さむ}い日は","どうしても","家に","こもりがちだ"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"On cold days I tend to stay indoors, whatever I do.", why:"〜がちだ ends it; 家に stays next to こもる."},
  {id:"b3-026", lv:"N3", tiles:["社長は","もう","お帰りに","なりました"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"The company president has already gone home.", why:"お〜になる (respectful) is split over two tiles and stays in order; もう goes before it."},
  {id:"b3-027", lv:"N3", tiles:["のちほど","こちらから","お電話","いたします"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3]], en:"We'll call you back later.", why:"お〜いたします (humble) ends it; のちほど and こちらから can swap."},
  {id:"b3-028", lv:"N3", tiles:["[昨日]{きのう}","先生が書かれた","[論文]{ろんぶん}を","はいけんしました"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,2,0,3]], en:"Yesterday I read the paper you wrote, Professor.", why:"先生が書かれた describes [論文]{ろんぶん}, so they stay together. [昨日]{きのう} can go first or before the verb."},
  {id:"b3-029", lv:"N3", tiles:["雨が[降]{ふ}っても","[試合]{しあい}は","[行]{おこな}われるそうだ"], orders:[[0,1,2],[1,0,2]], en:"I hear the match will go ahead even if it rains.", why:"The 〜ても clause and the topic can swap; 〜そうだ ends it."},
  {id:"b3-030", lv:"N3", tiles:["いくら","[説明]{せつめい}しても","分かって","もらえない"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"However much I explain, they don't understand.", why:"いくら〜ても = 'however much'; いくら comes first."},
  {id:"b3-031", lv:"N3", tiles:["[経験]{けいけん}が","なくても","できる","仕事です"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"It's a job you can do without experience.", why:"Everything before 仕事 describes it: [経験]{けいけん}がなくてもできる仕事."},
  {id:"b3-032", lv:"N3", tiles:["日本に来た","ばかりの","ころは","何もわからなかった"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"When I had just arrived in Japan, I didn't understand anything.", why:"た-form + ばかりの + noun: 'the time when I had just…'."},
  {id:"b3-033", lv:"N3", tiles:["一度","[約束]{やくそく}した","以上は","[守]{まも}るべきだ"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"Once you've made a promise, you should keep it.", why:"〜以上は = 'since, once'; the clause before it, the judgment (べきだ) after."},
  {id:"b3-034", lv:"N3", tiles:["[天気予報]{てんきよほう}によると","[明日]{あした}は","[雪]{ゆき}が[降]{ふ}るらしい"], orders:[[0,1,2],[1,0,2]], en:"According to the forecast, it's going to snow tomorrow.", why:"The source (〜によると) usually comes first, but it can follow the topic. 〜らしい ends it."},
  {id:"b3-035", lv:"N3", tiles:["同じ問題でも","人によって","意見が","[違]{ちが}う"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]], en:"Even on the same issue, opinions differ from person to person.", why:"〜でも first; 人によって can go before 意見が or right before [違]{ちが}う. The verb is last."},
  {id:"b3-036", lv:"N3", tiles:["[寝]{ね}る前に","スマホを","見ない","ようにしている"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3]], en:"I try not to look at my phone before bed.", why:"〜ようにしている ends it. The time clause and スマホを can swap."},
  {id:"b3-037", lv:"N3", tiles:["今から","急いで","行っても","間に[合]{あ}わないだろう"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[1,0,2,3]], en:"Even if we hurry and go now, we probably won't make it.", why:"〜ても clause first, then the result. 今から and 急いで can swap."},
  {id:"b3-038", lv:"N3", tiles:["[彼]{かれ}が","来るかどうか","まだ","わからない"], orders:[[0,1,2,3],[2,0,1,3]], en:"I still don't know whether he's coming.", why:"[彼]{かれ}が来るかどうか stays together. まだ goes before it or right before わからない."},
  {id:"b3-039", lv:"N3", tiles:["ドアを","開けた","とたんに","[猫]{ねこ}が[飛]{と}び出してきた"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"The moment I opened the door, the cat jumped out.", why:"た-form + とたんに = 'the moment'; the sudden event follows."},
  {id:"b3-040", lv:"N3", tiles:["来年の","春から","一人で","[暮]{く}らすことにした"], orders:[[0,1,2,3]], en:"I've decided to live on my own from next spring.", why:"来年の describes 春. 〜ことにした (decided) ends the sentence."}
]
};
